---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Home
description: "Daniel Brockwell: portfolio manager in digital assets at Nickel Digital Asset Management, who builds the tools behind the work. Outside work: record-setting computations, and software for Android and the Psion Organiser II."
---
{% import "components/ui.njk" as ui %}
<div class="wrap">
  <section class="hero hero-work">
    <div>
      <h1>{{ site.name }}</h1>
      <p class="kicker">Portfolio manager, digital assets</p>
      <p class="lede">I help run an eight-figure liquid digital-asset fund at Nickel Digital Asset Management, taking investment and trading ideas from research to execution, and I build the tools behind them. Outside work I run record-setting computations and write software for very small machines.</p>
      <p class="buttons">
        <a class="button" href="/cv/">CV</a>
        {% if "/downloads/cv/daniel-brockwell-cv.pdf" | fileExists %}<a class="button button-secondary" href="/downloads/cv/daniel-brockwell-cv.pdf" download>CV as PDF</a>{% endif %}
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Role</dt><dd>Portfolio Manager, Nickel Digital Asset Management, since November 2022</dd>
      <dt>Fund</dt><dd>Eight-figure, long-only, liquid digital assets</dd>
      <dt>In crypto since</dt><dd>January 2022, as a DeFi Analyst</dd>
      <dt>Regulation</dt><dd>FCA Certification Regime, client dealing (<a href="https://register.fca.org.uk/s/individual?id=003Sk00000kJM0oIAG">DXB01169</a>)</dd>
      <dt>Education</dt><dd>BSc Computer Science, 2:1, University of Sheffield</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <h2>My work</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-2">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="card-when mono">September 2022</p>
      <h3 class="card-title"><a href="/work/ethereum-merge/">The Ethereum Merge</a></h3>
      <p class="card-summary">Identified, developed and executed a profitable trade around the Merge, exploiting Aave's stale exchange rates on the proof-of-work fork.</p>
      <p class="card-actions"><a href="/work/ethereum-merge/">How the trade worked</a></p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="card-when mono">April 2024</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">An early warning on sUSD</h3>
      <p class="card-summary">My on-chain alerts flagged falling liquidity in Synthetix's sETH wrapper, and with it the risk of an sUSD depeg. The fund exited its sUSD exposure.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="card-when mono">Ongoing</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">Market making</h3>
      <p class="card-summary">I build and run market-making bots on venues including Hyperliquid: quoting both sides, managing inventory risk, mainly to earn exchange incentives.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="card-when mono">Ongoing</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">The fund's own on-chain data</h3>
      <p class="card-summary">A full Ethereum node, custom alerts for stablecoin depegs, large protocol withdrawals and high lending rates, and Tenderly simulation of transactions before they are sent.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p><a href="/cv/">Full experience, skills and education in my CV</a></p>

  <hr class="rule">
  <h2>Records</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-2">
    {%- for r in person.records %}
    <article class="card">
      <h3 class="card-title"><a href="{{ r.page }}">{{ r.text }}</a></h3>
      {{ ui.proof([{ label: r.source, url: r.url }]) }}
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <hr class="rule">
  <h2>Outside work</h2>
  <p class="prose">I like small, exact programs: a chess engine in 6303 machine code for a pocket computer from 1986, puzzle games for Android whose solvers prove every level can be solved without guessing, and long computations tuned until the hardware is the limit.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    {%- set psionCount = collections.programs | length %}
    {%- set androidCount = collections.projects | countIn("section", "android") %}
    {%- set personalCount = collections.projects | countIn("section", "personal") %}
    {%- for s in [
      ["Psion", "/psion/", "Games and utilities for the Organiser II, with downloads and source.", psionCount, "program"],
      ["Android", "/android/", "Apps and games for Android phones.", androidCount, "project"],
      ["Personal", "/personal/", "Record prime searches and computations of mathematical constants.", personalCount, "project"]
    ] %}
    <article class="card">
      <h3 class="card-title"><a href="{{ s[1] }}">{{ s[0] }}</a></h3>
      <p class="card-summary">{{ s[2] }}</p>
      <p class="count">{{ s[3] }} {{ s[4] }}{% if s[3] != 1 %}s{% endif %}</p>
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <h3>Latest</h3>
  <ul class="latest">
    {%- for e in collections.latest %}
    <li><a href="{{ e.url }}">{{ e.data.title }}</a> {{ ui.badge(e.data.status) }} <span class="small">updated <time datetime="{{ e.data.updated | dateIso }}">{{ e.data.updated | dateLong }}</time></span><br>{{ e.data.summary }}{% if e.data.proof %} <span class="small">(source: {% for l in e.data.proof %}<a href="{{ l.url }}">{{ l.label }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})</span>{% endif %}</li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/about/">More about me</a> · <a href="/feed.xml">RSS feed</a></p>
</div>
